.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/@socket.io/component-emitter Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "`@socket\&.io/component-emitter`"
.PP
Event emitter component\&.

.PP
This project is a fork of the \fR\fRcomponent-emitter\fP\fP project, with \fRSocket\&.IO\fP-specific TypeScript typings\&.
.SH "Installation"
.PP
.PP
.nf
$ npm i @socket\&.io/component\-emitter
.fi
.PP
.SH "API"
.PP
.SS "Emitter(obj)"
The \fREmitter\fP may also be used as a mixin\&. For example a "plain" object may become an emitter, or you may extend an existing prototype\&.

.PP
As an \fREmitter\fP instance:

.PP
.PP
.nf
import { Emitter } from '@socket\&.io/component\-emitter';

var emitter = new Emitter;
emitter\&.emit('something');
.fi
.PP

.PP
As a mixin:

.PP
.PP
.nf
import { Emitter } from '@socket\&.io/component\-emitter';

var user = { name: 'tobi' };
Emitter(user);

user\&.emit('im a user');
.fi
.PP

.PP
As a prototype mixin:

.PP
.PP
.nf
import { Emitter } from '@socket\&.io/component\-emitter';

Emitter(User\&.prototype);
.fi
.PP
.SS "Emitter#on(event, fn)"
Register an \fRevent\fP handler \fRfn\fP\&.
.SS "Emitter#once(event, fn)"
Register a single-shot \fRevent\fP handler \fRfn\fP, removed immediately after it is invoked the first time\&.
.SS "Emitter#off(event, fn)"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Pass \fRevent\fP and \fRfn\fP to remove a listener\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Pass \fRevent\fP to remove all listeners on that event\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Pass nothing to remove all listeners on all events\&.
.PP
.SS "Emitter#emit(event, \&.\&.\&.)"
Emit an \fRevent\fP with variable option args\&.
.SS "Emitter#listeners(event)"
Return an array of callbacks, or an empty array\&.
.SS "Emitter#hasListeners(event)"
Check if this emitter has \fRevent\fP handlers\&.
